{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WGqRLxJTNJQzrbXkdzVzvb","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 40c03647932e8f4a30f8671b21e82dabe0d932af\nAuthor: Patrick Devaney <patrickbdevaney@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 19 22:12:35 2026 -0400\n\n    1.6 resolved by control build; 1b.1 pack primitives gated bit-exact\n    \n    THE LAUNCH ERROR IS PRE-EXISTING, PROVEN BY EXPERIMENT. Built decode_prechange from\n    1a33cfe^ -- the two kernel files and the header as they were before the warp top-k -- and\n    ran it: err711=42, err820=21, the same fault. It has nothing to do with this work. I called\n    this wrong twice, first as mine and then as pre-existing on the strength of mla_attn.cu's\n    commit dates; both were reasoning from circumstance. The control build is the experiment\n    that settles it and it cost one model load, which is less than the two I spent probing.\n    \n    Still latent: output correct, LOSSLESS passes on every run including the control, tau\n    normal. The bs==1 kernel at the reporting site has no launch bounds, no static shared\n    memory and a 1024-block grid, so it cannot fail on its own -- the flag is stale from an\n    unprobed launch, plausibly a side stream. Tracked, not blocking.\n    \n    Free A/B from the control at ctx 480: base AR 92.6 -> 89.3 ms/tok, spec 67.2 -> 65.9.\n    Small at short context by construction, which is the point -- the win is the slope, and\n    0.2 measured that as flat.\n    \n    1b.1 PRIMITIVES. include/idx_pack.h stores the DSA index row as 128 E2M1 codes plus 4\n    UE8M0 scale bytes, 68 B against 512 B, 7.53x. This is lossless because the write path\n    already put every value on that grid: act_quant_fp4sim computes an exact power-of-two\n    scale and writes back round_e2m1(...) * scale, so packing keeps the code and the exponent\n    and unpacking recomputes the same product. Multiplying by a power of two is exact in IEEE\n    754. 68 B/token is also exactly what SGLang ships for the DeepSeek-V4 FP4 indexer pool.\n    \n    tests/gate_idx_pack.cu proves unpack(pack(x)) == x bit-for-bit on 524,288 elements across\n    tiny, large and zero-heavy distributions.\n    \n    THE GATE EARNED ITSELF ON THE FIRST RUN. The initial e2m1_code took the sign from ,\n    but round_e2m1 returns NEGATIVE ZERO when a negative input rounds to zero, and -0.0f < 0.0f\n    is false, so the sign was silently dropped: 16,011 mismatches at worst |delta| = 0.\n    Numerically perfect, bitwise wrong, and invisible to any tolerance-based check. This is the\n    argument for memcmp acceptance in one example.\n    \n    Wiring still to do: 6 allocation/memcpy sites bake in the 4-byte stride, plus the write\n    path and both index_score read kernels.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n DECODE_LADDER.md       | 58 +++++++++++++++++---------------\n include/idx_pack.h     | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/gate_idx_pack.cu | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 3 files changed, 202 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)\n=== build/decode vs HEAD sources ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    16780 08-12_00:39 kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd   110302 08-12_01:04 src/decode.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    26196 08-12_01:37 include/unicode_cat.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     5002 08-12_01:44 include/dsv4_load.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     4514 08-12_01:49 include/stream_parse.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    14828 08-12_01:52 include/webui_dsv4.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    17121 08-12_02:29 include/tokenizer_dsv4.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    38245 08-12_19:41 kernels/tc_moe_gemm.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     7998 08-13_05:14 include/openai_api.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     3327 08-13_12:05 include/compressed_decode.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    33246 08-13_12:14 kernels/compressor.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     4400 08-13_12:15 include/compressor.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    18906 08-13_12:15 kernels/block_decode.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     6167 08-15_12:58 include/dsv4_engine.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     4549 08-19_21:09 include/indexer.h\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    10838 08-19_21:09 kernels/indexer.cu\n-rwxrwxr-x 1 patrickd patrickd 17492408 08-19_21:25 build/decode\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    42712 08-19_22:02 kernels/compressed_decode.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd    42712 08-19_22:02 kernels/compressed_decode.cu\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 patrickd patrickd     4483 08-19_22:11 include/idx_pack.h","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43498f3c-c9c5-40d9-b79a-d6b785466892","uuid":"80904a93-1fb3-475d-9668-be609225b46d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:04:53.169Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 40c03647932e8f4a30f8671b21e82dabe0d932af\nAuthor: Patrick Devaney <patrickbdevaney@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 19 22:12:35 2026 -0400\n\n    1.6 resolved by control build; 1b.1 pack primitives gated bit-exact\n    \n    THE LAUNCH ERROR IS PRE-EXISTING, PROVEN BY EXPERIMENT. Built decode_prechange from\n    1a33cfe^ -- the two kernel files and the header as they were before the warp top-k -- and\n    ran it: err711=42, err820=21, the same fault. It has nothing to do with this work. I called\n    this wrong twice, first as mine and then as pre-existing on the strength of mla_attn.cu's\n    commit dates; both were reasoning from circumstance. The control build is the experiment\n    that settles it and it cost one model load, which is less than the two I spent probing.\n    \n    Still latent: output correct, LOSSLESS passes on every run including the control, tau\n    normal. The bs==1 kernel at the reporting site has no launch bounds, no static shared\n    memory and a 1024-block grid, so it cannot fail on its own -- the flag is stale from an\n    unprobed launch, plausibly a side stream. Tracked, not blocking.\n 