{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDbhWpQD43AzHuqmpwNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016PL8FiaGADSbYztQhjarsa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda\ngrep -n '^#\\{1,3\\} ' wiki/measurement-and-traps.md\necho \"=== tail ===\"; tail -30 wiki/measurement-and-traps.md\necho \"=== kernel-opt headings ===\"; grep -n '^#\\{1,3\\} ' wiki/kernel-optimisations.md","description":"Read wiki structure"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4006,"cache_read_input_tokens":119480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4006},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d70d126-0070-4925-875e-05d6ca119884","uuid":"3f8eae02-d2ca-4b8c-af71-2ffc888ea408","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:23:13.695Z","request_id":"req_011CeDbhVSYdhHY9kgQapkDV"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016PL8FiaGADSbYztQhjarsa","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Measurement methodology, and the traps that earned it\n8:## 1. How a number becomes trustworthy here\n25:## 2. The trap that created rule 2\n32:## 3. The trap that created rule 3\n42:## 4. The traps that created rule 6\n52:## 5. The probe-distribution trap\n64:## 6. Counting the wrong quantity\n75:## 7. Host time is not critical-path time\n80:## 8. Instruments that cannot see themselves\n95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n=== tail ===\n\n## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n\n`dprof_report` has a parent/child consistency check. It fires an `*** INVALID` on the prefill table\nbecause `DP_C_COMPRESS` was assigned to a region *outside* `DP_ATTN` — an artifact of an id choice,\nnot an inconsistency (the 99.98 % accounting settles it). **It was left firing**, because that same\ncheck is what exposed the first run's missing marks.\n\n## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n\n- **`pgrep -f <script>` matches the shell running the grep** — reported \"executor RUNNING\" twice\n  while idle. Use `pgrep -x` or the lock the process actually holds.\n- **The auditor reviewed a sha and pushed a ref.** `HEAD_SHA` was captured at the top, checks ran\n  against it, then `git push origin main` published *whatever HEAD had become* — shipping a commit\n  it never reviewed. The audit log recorded the contradiction in its own entry (header sha from the\n  audit, subject line from a different commit) and read as normal. Now pushes the reviewed object.\n- **A documented manual workaround for a harness bug is not a mitigation if the harness runs last.**\n  The executor correctly hand-set a counter; the harness clobbered it thirty seconds later, leaving\n  a state note describing a value no longer in the file.\n- **An arena constant fitted to the 6-token gate prompt became a silent prompt-length ceiling** —\n  invisible because the gate prompt never reaches it (F62's shape, twice).\n\n## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n\n**Trap 1, and the origin of several others.** The canonical prompt is 6 tokens (`PSp=5`). It cannot\nreach any `bs>16` code path — which is exactly how F62 (garbage prefill for every prompt ≥18 tokens)\nsurvived every gate in the project.\n\n`gate_prefill_len` now varies length deliberately. **A masked read is not a safe read**: F62's row\nmasks made the reads legal and hid a missing loop.\n=== kernel-opt headings ===\n1:# Kernel optimisations — AR and speculative decode\n11:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n17:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n40:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n53:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n64:## 2. Structural wins\n66:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n75:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n90:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n99:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n106:## 3. Precision and layout\n120:## 4. What every adopted change has in common","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d70d126-0070-4925-875e-05d6ca119884","uuid":"4b1f4791-d4a3-4933-a2ab-88e9712712de","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:23:13.767Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Measurement methodology, and the traps that earned it\n8:## 1. How a number becomes trustworthy here\n25:## 2. The trap that created rule 2\n32:## 3. The trap that created rule 3\n42:## 4. The traps that created rule 6\n52:## 5. The probe-distribution trap\n64:## 6. Counting the wrong quantity\n75:## 7. Host time is not critical-path time\n80:## 8. Instruments that cannot see themselves\n95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n=== tail ===\n\n## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n\n`dprof_report` has a parent/child consistency check. It fires an `*** INVALID` on the prefill table\nbecause `DP_C_COMPRESS` was assigned to a region *outside* `DP_ATTN` — an artifact of an id choice,\nnot an inconsistency (the 99.98 % accounting settles it). **It was left firing**, because that same\ncheck is what exposed the first run's missing marks.\n\n## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n\n- **`pgrep -f <script>` matches the shell running the grep** — reported \"executor RUNNING\" twice\n  while idle. Use `pgrep -x` or the lock the process actually holds.\n- **The auditor reviewed a sha and pushed a ref.** `HEAD_SHA` was captured at the top, checks ran\n  against it, then `git push origin main` published *whatever HEAD had become* — shipping a commit\n  it never reviewed. The audit log recorded the contradiction in its own entry (header sha from the\n  audit, subject line from a different commit) and read as normal. Now pushes the reviewed object.\n- **A documented manual workaround for a harness bug is not a mitigation if the harness runs last.**\n  The executor correctly hand-set a counter; the harness clobbered it thirty seconds later, leaving\n  a state note describing a value no longer in the file.\n- **An arena constant fitted to the 6-token gate prompt became a silent prompt-length ceiling** —\n  invisible because the gate prompt never reaches it (F62's shape, twice).\n\n## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n\n**Trap 1, and the origin of several others.** The canonical prompt is 6 tokens (`PSp=5`). It cannot\nreach any `bs>16` code path — which is exactly how F62 (garbage prefill for every prompt ≥18 tokens)\nsurvived every gate in the project.\n\n`gate_prefill_len` now varies length deliberately. **A masked read is not a safe read**: F62's row\nmasks made the reads legal and hid a missing loop.\n=== kernel-opt headings ===\n1:# Kernel optimisations — AR and speculative decode\n11:## 1. The transformations tha