{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PTiGD9EctefMjFzvvqSwUc","type":"tool_result","content":"## Hard invariants — the loop must never violate these\n\n1. **Bit-exactness or an explicit gate.** Any kernel change either produces byte-identical generated\n   token ids, or ships behind the LOSSLESS gate with the deviation measured and recorded. A change\n   that silently alters output is reverted, not debugged.\n2. **tau is reported in every A/B.** A byte-identical token sequence can still collapse acceptance\n   3.12 -> 1.00 (`LOOP_LOG`), because acceptance is an exact draft/target comparison. Throughput\n   without tau is not a measurement.\n3. **Never restart the eval battery.** The watchdog and boot unit are disarmed on purpose. The GPU\n   is single-tenant; a second client turns a scored item into a banked wrong answer.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d70d126-0070-4925-875e-05d6ca119884","uuid":"dba9c9b1-83a8-4f93-a52e-0ed6bc9c8423","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:27:28.392Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Hard invariants — the loop must never violate these\n\n1. **Bit-exactness or an explicit gate.** Any kernel change either produces byte-identical generated\n   token ids, or ships behind the LOSSLESS gate with the deviation measured and recorded. A change\n   that silently alters output is reverted, not debugged.\n2. **tau is reported in every A/B.** A byte-identical token sequence can still collapse acceptance\n   3.12 -> 1.00 (`LOOP_LOG`), because acceptance is an exact draft/target comparison. Throughput\n   without tau is not a measurement.\n3. **Never restart the eval battery.** The watchdog and boot unit are disarmed on purpose. The GPU\n   is single-tenant; a second client turns a scored item into a banked wrong answer.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDc2oUYH2NL5pSb9nTFd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0178VsNybYfsugxUeweeqCEX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='DECODE_LADDER.md'\ns=open(p).read()\n\nold_inv = \"\"\"1. **Bit-exactness or an explicit gate.** Any kernel change either produces byte-identical generated\n   token ids, or ships behind the LOSSLESS gate with the deviation measured and recorded. A change\n   that silently alters output is reverted, not debugged.\n\"\"\"\nnew_inv = \"\"\"1. **Bit-exactness or an explicit gate.** Any kernel change either produces byte-identical generated\n   token ids, or ships behind the LOSSLESS gate with the deviation measured and recorded. A change\n   that silently alters output is reverted, not debugged.\n\n   **AMENDED 2026-08-20 by 1.0 — token ids are not a valid test at context, and this invariant was\n   nearly used to revert a correct change.** The engine does not reproduce itself run-to-run above\n   ctx ~1024: `build/decode` with `DSV4_MAINKV_CACHE=0` on **both** sides of the comparison, argmax,\n   no seed, no HTTP, still diverged from itself at the identical id index 1067. The cached path\n   never ran on either side, so the divergence cannot be the cache. **A token-id comparison is only\n   evidence if the same-arm control was run and passed — run the control FIRST.** Where it fails,\n   the invariant is satisfied instead by memcmp of the changed kernel's **entire output buffer**\n   against the untouched reference, in situ, on every call; that is strictly stronger, because it\n   proves the whole intermediate identical rather than one downstream consumer's output. See\n   `wiki/measurement-and-traps.md` §12 and item 1.9.\n\"\"\"\nassert old_inv in s\ns = s.replace(old_inv, new_inv)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY","description":"Amend invariant 1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":418,"cache_read_input_tokens":150579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":418},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d70d126-0070-4925-875e-05d6ca119884","uuid":"cfd8f83f-0b68-4898-9a4e-5cb2fffaef64","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:27:36.857Z","request_id":"req_011CeDc2nZiUxD3zSCsvVgMU"}
