{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDeCSo6RwNeMpQokFarc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean — that earlier \"STILL RUNNING\" was `pgrep -f` matching its own shell, which is precisely the trap documented in this repo's `measurement-and-traps.md` §10.\n\n## Iteration 1 complete — ladder item 1.0\n\n**The engine is faster: +24.4 % tok/s at ctx 12,282** (7.67 → 9.54), +21.7 % at 9,213, +15.8 % at 6,132.\n\n**What I found on arrival.** A previous iteration (killed by timeout) had already implemented the kernel and run the A/B, but left it unresolved: the log said `gate probe rc=1 … FATAL: bit-exactness gate did not pass cleanly` and 21 of 52 token-id legs differed. Both turned out to be false alarms, and establishing that was most of the work.\n\n- The gate had **passed** — 384 checks, 2,023,320 retained rows, 0 FAIL. What returned 1 was `decode_fit_probe.py`, correctly refusing to bank 32-token completions. The harness conflated *the carrier failed to collect timings* with *the thing being gated is broken*.\n- The 21 differing legs were **not the cache**. A second baseline sweep from an independent server start differs from the first on **the same 21 legs** — same set, both symmetric differences empty — with the cached path never executing on either side. `build/decode` reproduces the result with `DSV4_MAINKV_CACHE=0` on both sides.\n\n**Measurement.** The two arms produced bit-identical `tau` and verify width rep-for-rep at ctx ≥ 1536, so I compared paired rather than by medians: bands of ±1 % against the 3.5 % run-to-run spread. The saving regresses to **3.604 ± 0.076 ms per 1000 context** against the **3.867 ± 0.001** dprof had attributed to `draft:main_kv` — 93 % of it, and the 2 SE band does *not* cover the prediction. I recorded that 0.26 ms/1000 shortfall rather than rounding it into agreement. The null control (baseline vs baseline) reads 0.998–1.000× where the real A/B reads 1.267×.\n\n**Bit-exactness** rests on memcmp of the whole `[s, HEAD_DIM]` buffer: 704 calls, two binaries, 2.59 M retained rows, 0 FAIL. `build_gate.sh` asserted two negative controls that didn't exist in the test, so I built and ran them. Both fail the gate — and the GEMM-pin control fails on **377 of 1,048,576 floats at the last ulp, only at `g_tc_fp8=1`**, which is exactly what a tolerance check waves through, on the only path decode uses.\n\n**The finding I'd flag as most consequential beyond this item:** the engine does not reproduce itself once a run is long enough, so the ladder's \"byte-identical generated token ids\" invariant is untestable past that point. I amended hard invariant 1 (run the same-arm control *first*; fall back to buffer memcmp, which is stronger anyway) and opened item **1.9** — ranked deliberately *below* the two remaining kernel changes, since the buffer gate is a working substitute and this ladder has already overspent on instruments.\n\nWiki updated in the same iteration: `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.5, `context-scaling.md`, `measurement-and-traps.md` §12–13, `README.md` state table (every row now carries a context).\n\nTwo things to note: I could not commit or push — project policy denies `git add`/`commit`/`push` for me, so the loop driver commits from `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p0.txt`, which I've written. And I shortened the verify prompts from 6,132 to 3,072 tokens, because `build/decode` allocates ~2.99 MB per `seqmax` token and the first attempt was memguard-killed at MemAvailable 219 MB; the depth claim rests on the in-situ gate at 12,281 rows instead, and I added a `DSV4_PARSE_ONLY` pre-gate so that failure costs milliseconds rather than a 100 GiB load."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":184,"cache_read_input_tokens":207105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":184},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d70d126-0070-4925-875e-05d6ca119884","uuid":"f72a0b65-02f7-49b4-a008-edf6a29c5286","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:56:14.865Z","request_id":"req_011CeDeCQxxpu97EFcbTQZ3y"}
