{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEBsT2vsijDTHcXU9nS8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The repo denies `git add/commit/push` to me — the loop driver commits on the iteration's behalf from a prepared message file. Writing it:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":157295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":834},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29339add-fefb-4fb1-8cb9-c27015f0e898","uuid":"1c77097e-95d9-4b50-a77b-66c29fc062b4","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:51:16.954Z","request_id":"req_011CeEBsRwwSe6S6ozP4kpXA"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEBsT2vsijDTHcXU9nS8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MwMtp4K7HpkKrTjfqmwC8d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda\ncat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p2.txt <<'EOF'\n2.2: deploy s3 -- tau 3.5362 -> 3.8438 and +9.52 % tok/s on the frozen suite, and the server has now actually run it\n\ns3 was promoted 2026-08-12 and had never been loaded by a server. promote_head.py archives and\ndeliberately never writes the live checkpoint; scripts/serve.sh -- which every launcher in this repo\nexecs -- hardcoded the base checkpoint path. So the promotion pipeline terminated one step short of\nhaving any effect, for eight days. A head nobody serves is not a speedup.\n\nMECHANISM: a staged checkpoint, not a --head flag, and src/engine.cu is the argument. All 2977 mtp.*\ntensors are EMBEDDED in shards 46-48 and those shards hold nothing else, which is why the engine\nreads the head out of the main WeightStore -- a second store \"would duplicate ~6.5 GiB against\n~16 GiB of headroom\". A flag ADDS a mapping; staging REPLACES one. scripts/stage_head.sh builds\n~/models/ckpt-head-s3 as a symlink farm: 45 shards, tokenizer and config linked to the read-only\nbase at the SAME INODE, the three head shards linked to the archive. Resident set is bit-for-bit a\nproduction load, the checkpoint is never written, no disk is spent, and the A/B runs an identical\nbinary. config/live_ckpt -- tracked, one line -- is the single switch serve.sh reads.\n\ntools/verify_staged_ckpt.py gates it on the CPU in seconds, before ten minutes of weight load:\n45,821/45,821 tensors drop-in identical in dtype/shape/byte-length; 45 files the same inode as base;\nthe 3 head shards' sha256 equal to what head_card.json recorded at promotion, so what is served is\nprovably the artifact that was measured; and the head shards proven DIFFERENT from base -- a no-op\nstage would have measured the shipped head twice and called it a deployment.\n\nMEASURED. The archived numbers (rev 85dbea6c / 2632540) predate 1.0/1.2/1.3/1.4/1.5 and are not an\nadmissible before-arm, so both heads were re-measured back to back on 93699e6, same binary, frozen\nprotocol (8-prompt suite, block 6, adaptK 1.50, NGEN0 200, clean, cache dropped before each).\nLOSSLESS GATE PASS and first-token GATE PASS on both arms.\n\n                 base AR   suite tau   suite tok/s   tok/s / base AR\n  shipped        11.41     3.5362      22.1425       1.9406\n  s3             11.33     3.8438      24.2512       2.1404\n  delta          -0.70 %   +0.3076     +9.52 %       +10.30 %\n                           (+8.70 %)\n\nThe -0.70 % on base AR is the drift control: base AR never touches the draft head, so it measures\nthe between-load spread (5.7 % per traps §19) that per-prompt pairing cannot cancel. Paired per\nprompt: d tau = +0.3075 +/- 0.4814, 5/8 legs positive -- and that band is NOT measurement error, it\nis between-PROMPT heterogeneity, because tau is exact. Decided on this corpus; weakly established on\nan arbitrary prompt.\n\nWHAT IMPROVED IS THE FLOOR, NOT THE CEILING. Per-prompt tau shipped 5.15 4.43 1.84 1.75 5.54 4.46\n1.85 3.27 -> s3 3.64 4.20 2.49 3.06 3.94 6.09 3.85 3.48. The three prompts where the shipped head\nbarely speculated at all (tau < 2 of a possible 5) are the three largest gains; after s3 no suite\nprompt is below 2; s.d. across the suite falls 1.570 -> 1.056 (-32.8 %) while the mean rises; prompt\n7 goes 14.39 -> 26.33 tok/s, +83 %, which no suite mean will ever show. On real work the worst\nprompts dominate wall-clock, so mean tau understates this.\n\nPROVEN LIVE, NOT ASSERTED. Server started via run_server.sh (detached, ppid systemd, tty ?,\ndetach_audit green), log shows \"live checkpoint pinned by config/live_ckpt -> .../ckpt-head-s3\", and\na completion on the gate prompt returned tokens_per_verify = 2.857 -- against the shipped head's\n3.61 and s3's 2.87 for that same prompt offline. Behavioural proof of which weights are resident,\nnot a path in a log line. Server then stopped: the deployment is the tracked pointer file, not a\nrunning process, and 100 GiB resident would block the next iteration.\n\nTWO FINDINGS THIS TURNED UP, QUEUED AS 2.4 AND 2.5 RATHER THAN FOLDED IN:\n\n  2.4  promote_head.py's docstring criterion 4 says \"suite-mean TAU must exceed the incumbent's by\n       3.5 %\"; the code compares suite_tok_s, against an incumbent row recorded on a DIFFERENT\n       engine revision. This iteration measured that axis directly: suite tau reproduced the\n       archived value to FOUR DECIMAL PLACES for both heads across 8 days and five kernel rewrites,\n       while suite tok/s moved -2.3 % and -5.0 % and base AR moved -17.4 %. s2 was refused by a\n       2.5 % margin on exactly this comparison. Three of seven registry rows are verdicts of this\n       shape and one of the refused heads may already beat s3.\n\n  2.5  base AR fell 72.5 -> 87.7/88.2 ms/tok on the identical WARM decode measurement, twice, in two\n       independent loads. Do NOT call it a 17 % regression yet: spec throughput on the same suite in\n       the same runs is flat, and spec runs the same forward. Likeliest a 7-step warm average that\n       is too short for a path 1.0 put a cache on. Either way every \"N.NNx vs base AR\" figure in\n       this repo has a denominator that moved 17 % while its numerator did not.\n\nWiki, same commit: kernel-optimisations.md §2.8 (the one adopted win that is not a kernel),\ndraft-head-finetuning.md §8 (mechanism, measurement, floor-not-ceiling), measurement-and-traps.md\n§22 (tau reproduces exactly, tok/s does not, and the gate keys on the wrong one),\nHEAD_REGISTRY.md \"What is actually being served\", README state table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nwc -l evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p2.txt; ls -t evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_*.txt","description":"Write the prepared commit message for the driver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":157295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":834},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29339add-fefb-4fb1-8cb9-c27015f0e898","uuid":"8b9f5d46-37a1-412d-ad74-495a88002043","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:51:45.271Z","request_id":"req_011CeEBsRwwSe6S6ozP4kpXA"}
